      "title": "Unconditional test cleanup discards restart and failure evidence",
      "evidence": "Directory::drop calls remove_dir_all unconditionally. Every new filesystem test owns Directory. sample writes PID-named stdout/stderr into this directory; the positive restart case also places both snapshots and finite-baseline.emf.staged there.",
      "counterexample": "A full persisted oracle or PID assertion fails after writer/read execution. Ordinary panic unwinding runs Drop and removes the very raw logs/snapshots needed to inspect the failure. A successful no-overwrite case asserts failed staging retained at201\u2013204, then immediately removes that staging file and both process logs when the test exits.",
      "impact": "No post-run raw test artifact survives success or ordinary assertion failure. In-memory assertions are useful but cannot supply the stated retained process/raw-byte evidence.",
      "needed_verification": "After formal registration and a fresh authorized source lease, define evidence custody for each test attempt and retain or archive exact logs, snapshots and failed staging on Samsung before removal. Demonstrate an intentional assertion-failure attempt leaves inspectable bounded output, PIDs and bytes, and a normal success leaves reviewable evidence. Preserve original166 donor and every existing assertion/case.",
      "certainty": "Confirmed source behavior; counterexample not executed."
    },
    {
      "id": "RT04-02",
      "priority": "P2",
      "kind": "missing_critical_cli_no_overwrite_case",
      "file": "tests/finite_import_restart.rs",
      "line_start": 186,
      "line_end": 204,
      "title": "CLI rerun cannot exercise collision at the final snapshot key",
      "evidence": "The test creates both finite.emf.json and finite-baseline.emf.json in the first writer. It directly calls save_new(\"finite\") at186\u2013190, then reruns the CLI at192. The CLI saves finite-baseline at examples/import_save_reopen.rs136 before saving finite at158.",
      "counterexample": "A future regression keeps baseline save_new correct but replaces final-key publication with an overwrite. The first writer still succeeds on fresh storage. The direct SnapshotStore test still refuses overwrite. The negative CLI rerun fails on the existing baseline at136 and never reaches the regressed final save158. Every current assertion can pass.",
      "impact": "The current test establishes a baseline-key CLI refusal and direct final-key SnapshotStore refusal, but does not establish CLI refusal for an existing final key when baseline creation can proceed.",
      "needed_verification": "After formal registration and fresh authorized source lease, retain all existing cases and add an isolated existing-final/absent-baseline namespace. Run writer, assert refusal and unchanged preexisting final bytes, inspect retained stage/log evidence and confirm a fresh reader still loads the prior final. Count all additions normally.",
      "certainty": "Confirmed control-flow/coverage gap; current final CLI call is correctly save_new and no production overwrite observed."
    }
